# Resolution: Fix Node 20 deprecation warning, nanoid vuln, and bump pnpm in hyrperchess-core CI

## Validation Checklist
- [x] Verify `pnpm/action-setup@v6`'s action.yml declares `using: node24` (vs v4's `node20`)
- [x] Verify CI green after action-setup bump (run 34843353451: success)
- [x] Verify `pnpm audit --prod --audit-level high` clean locally after nanoid override
- [x] Verify `pnpm run build` clean across all 6 workspace packages after nanoid override
- [x] Verify CI + Security audit both green after nanoid fix (runs 34863741435, 34863741455: success)
- [x] Verify `pnpm audit`, `pnpm run build`, and full test suite (72/72 tests) clean under pnpm 12.4.1
- [x] Verify CI + Security audit both green after pnpm bump (runs 34988213019, 34988212983: success)
- [x] Verify both `github` and `gitlab` remotes are in sync on `main` after every push

## Outcomes / Summary
All three fixes landed on `hyrperchess-core`'s `main` branch, pushed to both `github` and `gitlab`
remotes, and verified green in CI end to end:

1. `ci: bump pnpm/action-setup to v6 to fix Node 20 deprecation warning` (5dae05f)
2. `fix(deps): override nanoid to patch high-severity DoS vulnerability` (9b5a39b)
3. `docs: add session dev report ...` (78a8262)
4. `chore(deps): bump pnpm to 12.4.1` (0ae566e)
5. `docs: update session dev report with pnpm 12.4.1 bump` (69c870b)

Full narrative, root causes, and decisions of record are in the session dev report:
`docs/dev-reports/20260914-191338-dev-report.md` (also committed inside `hyrperchess-core` at the
same path).

**Process note:** this todo trio was created retroactively, after the work was already complete,
because the task_management.md trio-creation step was skipped at session start. Future sessions
should create the trio as step one, even for what looks like a small reactive CI fix.
